tellraw @a {"text": "Technology: The heavy plough, the horse collar and three-field rotation", "color": "gold", "bold": true}
tellraw @a {"text": "Three open fields in rotation with a heavy plough and collared horse.", "color": "white"}
tellraw @a {"text": "Medieval Europe, heavy plough spreading from the 7th century; padded horse collar by the 10th; three-field system from the 8th-9th century", "color": "yellow"}
tellraw @a {"text": "The wheeled mouldboard plough cut and turned the heavy clay soils of the north that the", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "Mediterranean scratch plough could not; the rigid horse collar let horses pull it at full", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "strength; rotating winter grain, spring crop and fallow raised output by a third and", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "spread the work through the year.", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "A coulter slices the sod, the share cuts beneath it and the mouldboard turns it over,", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "burying weeds and draining the furrow. The collar bears on the horse's shoulders instead", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "of its windpipe. In three-field rotation each year a third of the land lies fallow and is", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "grazed, returning manure.", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "See it in context: /function ac:viking/ravensthorpe", "color": "aqua"}
